<id/06/0683/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Senna"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "the leaflets of several species of *Cassia*, used in medicine for their purgative properties. *C. elongata* and *C. acutifolia*, furnish the Timnevelly and Alexandrian senna, which are the best. The latter constitutes the bulk of the imports into Europe. It is much adulterated with the leaves of *Cynanchum Argel*, *Tephrosia Apollinea*, and *Coriaria myrtifolia*. Our imports average about 150,000 lbs, although they are often much larger. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 348]"@en ;
